                            "transitive"
                        ],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "861d7274-df8e-32c3-ac33-8d75479dbb6c",
                        "entry_id": "ca0ad343-2fd9-3c48-9a98-4aa5081e707f",
                        "glosses": [
                            "To talk privately or secretly; to conspire."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "rare"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "39f22803-89a7-4307-9a1c-d8b61e14fbc6",
                                "sense_id": "861d7274-df8e-32c3-ac33-8d75479dbb6c",
                                "text": "And then it seems that she collogued with her master and heard word of a subtler device."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a74f09e8-c7c1-4d4c-abaf-72879fc197d8",
                                "sense_id": "861d7274-df8e-32c3-ac33-8d75479dbb6c",
                                "text": "\"I see him,\" said the housemaid. \"He was colloguing with the butcher in the yard a bit since. He'd got a brown-paper parcel. Perhaps he got a lift home.\""
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "a3624299-9729-4d73-be41-4bfb8a2d212e",
                                "sense_id": "861d7274-df8e-32c3-ac33-8d75479dbb6c",
                                "text": "Ay, well, what I say - \" Flusky frowned, endeavouring to put into words just what he did say, when he collogued with his own thoughts. \"What I say: in a country where everything's to do, the hands has a chance to put themselves equal with the head.\""
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "79c0f55d-8c6e-4fbf-9e29-2c1fedca1e3e",
                                "sense_id": "861d7274-df8e-32c3-ac33-8d75479dbb6c",
                                "text": "You let Dunsey have it, sir? And how long have you been so thick with Dunsey that you must collogue with him to embezzle my money?"
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "3bb7e82b-6142-42aa-9460-027eb5f0bca5",
                                "sense_id": "861d7274-df8e-32c3-ac33-8d75479dbb6c",
                                "text": "Witch Hunter: You dare to collogue about me with such a [contemnible] manner of speech?!"
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
